┌───────────────────────────┐
│ Quick Introduction        │
│                           │
│ Uniform acceleration      │  
│ occurs when an object’s   │
│ velocity changes by equal │
│ amounts in equal time     │
│ intervals. This means the │
│ acceleration remains      │
│ constant throughout motion.│
└───────────────────────────┘

---

┌───────────────────────────┐
│ Key Definition            │
│                           │
│ **Uniform acceleration**  │
│ is acceleration that does │
│ not change in magnitude   │
│ or direction over time.   │
│                           │
│ This results in a         │
│ steady increase (or       │
│ decrease) in velocity.    │
└───────────────────────────┘

---

┌───────────────────────────┐
│ Core Characteristic       │
│                           │
│ - Constant rate of        │
│   change in velocity      │
│ - Straight-line motion    │
│   (usually)               │
│ - Velocity-time graph is  │
│   a straight line         │
│ - Position-time graph is  │
│   parabolic               │
└──────────────── classified───┘

---

$$
a = \frac{\Delta v}{\Delta t}
$$

┌───────────────────────────┐
│ Main Formula              │
│                           │
│     $$a = \frac{\Delta v}│
│            {\Delta t}$$   │
│                           │
│ [ Explain Formula ]       │
│ [ Open Formula Lab ]      │
└───────────────────────────┘

> **Where:**  
> - $ a $ = acceleration (m/s²)  
> - $ \Delta v $ = change in velocity (m/s)  
> - $ \Delta t $ = time interval (s)

This formula defines **average acceleration**, but under uniform acceleration, average and instantaneous acceleration are equal.

---

$$
v = u + at
$$

┌───────────────────────────┐
│ Velocity-Time Formula     │
│                           │
│     $$v = u + at$$        │
│                           │
│ [ Explain Formula ]       │
│ [ Open Formula Lab ]      │
└───────────────────────────┘

> **Where:**  
> - $ v $ = final velocity  
> - $ u $ = initial velocity  
> - $ a $ = uniform acceleration  
> - $ t $ = time

This equation calculates the final velocity of an object under uniform acceleration.

---

$$
s = ut + \frac{1}{2}at^2
$$

┌───────────────────────────┐
│ Displacement Formula      │
│                           │
│     $$s = ut + \frac{1}{2│
│           }at^2$$          │
│                           │
│ [ Explain Formula ]       │
│ [ Open Formula Lab ]      │
└───────────────────────────┘

> **Where:**  
> - $ s $ = displacement  
> - $ u $ = initial velocity  
> - $ a $ = acceleration  
> - $ t $ = time

This gives the position of an object at time $ t $ under uniform acceleration.

